  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Auction Forty-Fives. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Auction Forty-Fives (45s, Nova Scotia style) is a partnership trick game: 4 or 6 players, 5 cards each plus 4-card kitty. Bid in 5s (min 15-20); high bidder declares trump and may exchange with kitty. First team to 120 wins. Trump: 5 highest, then J, then A of hearts (always trump). Each trick 5 points; highest trump in trick +5. Special: 30 for 60 (win all tricks); 60 for 120 when below zero. Pagat spoil5/45; regional rules vary.',
    objective: 'First team to 120 points. Bid in 5s; high bidder declares trump, may use kitty.',
    gameplay: 'Follow suit when trump led; else any. Trick = 5 pts; highest trump in trick +5. 30 for 60 = all tricks (60 if made, 30 if not); 60 for 120 only when team below zero. House rules vary.',
